   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "id": "t2",
   "text": "Kessler syndrome. One satellite collision could cascade into debris that seals us on this planet.",
   "vis": {
    "t": "ice",
    "tier": 1
   },
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "id": "t3",
   "text": "The Great Filter. Something may stop civilisations before they spread. Nobody knows if it is behind us, or ahead.",
   "vis": {
    "t": "ice",
    "tier": 2
   },
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "id": "t4",
   "text": "Heat death. If physics holds, energy spreads out evenly until nothing can ever happen again.",
   "vis": {
    "t": "ice",
    "tier": 3
   },
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "id": "t5",
   "text": "And Boltzmann brains. The idea that random noise makes lone conscious minds more likely than whole universes.",
